script:post-response {
  // Get the 'X-Entity-Id' header from the response
  let person3Id = res.headers["x-entity-id"];
  
  // If the header exists, store it as an environment variable
  if (person3Id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("person3Id", person3Id);
  }
  
}

tests {
  // postman.setGlobalVariable("person3Id", res.getHeader("X-Entity-Id"));
}

docs {
  The /tree/persons endpoint creates a new person record based on the information provided in the Request Body. The request body specifies the Tree Id of the new CET tree created in Step (1-2).
  
  This request demostrates adding a new person to the CET tree based on the currently selected tree. Note that no treeId is provided in the request body.
  
  This request in the collection persists the Person Id as person3Id in the global variables. This person ID will be used in the creation of relationships in Steps (4-1) and (4-2).
  
  If the status code from this request is 201 Created, proceed to (2-6) Set Current Tree to GLOBAL
}
